# Desktop wiring for x-host-live-control (applied by the wave's DESKTOP-WIRE task)

[host/connection.ts] HOST_METHOD: no row needed (browser-live-control.ts holds the method name itself); HOST_CAPABILITIES.browser is already true.

[host/index.ts] in createDesktopHost, beside the other register*Host(connection, ...) calls:
  import { registerBrowserLiveControlHost } from './browser-live-control';
  registerBrowserLiveControlHost(connection, () => <the browser remote control from createRemoteControl: its { resize, widenVideo }>);
The control is resolved lazily (the callback runs per request) because the remote control is created after the host connection.
